<SddMigrationV1V2 keywords="migration, v1, v2, upgrade, tasks-to-specs, task-id, slug, anchors, compression, decision-merge, restructure, plan-first, sdd-migration" type="directive" ver="2.0">
  <Mission>
    Migrate a repo from the SDD v1 layout to v2 — interactively, plan-first, under git (baseline first —
    every step is revertible). Entered when
    `sdd-state` reports `FLOW_VERSION=v1` (a `tasks/` directory), from the router preflight or any door.
    This is a SPECIFIC v1→v2 directive; a later `v2→v3` is its own sibling. Self-sufficient: it may run
    without the router core, so it repeats the operator-facing axioms it needs.

    Not a mechanical copy. Changing decisions changes their references in code, so the migration reads and
    touches code, and it compresses: decisions and discussion threads that converged on the same thing
    during the document's evolution are collapsed (the compression protocol is loaded lazily). The
    operator first sees the whole plan — current → target, how many passes, what moves where, which IDs
    change, which decisions merge, which files are touched, what gets optimized — and acknowledges it
    before anything is written.

    Input — a v1 repo + the `sdd-migrate` / `sdd-state` / `sdd-check` tools. Output — a v2 repo
    (co-located `specs/`, slug Task-IDs, anchored tickets, compressed decisions, flat-Russian prose)
    that passes `sdd-state` v2 + `sdd-check` clean. Out of scope: authoring new specs (the scope/module
    branches) — migration only transforms what already exists.
  </Mission>

