  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECTS_PLAN` | Operator declines the migration plan — stop; nothing is written |
    | `H_NOT_V1` | `sdd-state` does not report `FLOW_VERSION=v1` — there is nothing to migrate; return control |
    | `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL` | Final verification cannot reach v2 + clean and the gap is not recoverable in-flow — stop, report state, leave git baseline for rollback |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_SCAN">
      <Goal>Inventory the v1 repo deterministically — the raw material for the plan.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Confirm `FLOW_VERSION=v1` via `sdd-state` (else `H_NOT_V1`). Gather, with tools, not by eye:
        `sdd-migrate anchors --all` (DRY-RUN — which tickets would be anchored / already are); the ticket
        set under `tasks/<scope>/<module>/*.task-*.md`; the Task-ID families and their counts
        (`TSK-NN` / `<ACR>-NNN`); the decision IDs (`D-NNN`) and where they repeat; the scope/module
        shape from the `tasks/` tree + portal. No writes here.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_PLAN">
      <Goal>Show the operator the whole migration before touching anything.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Build and present the plan, in plain Russian (`AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE`), across as many messages as
        it needs to be clear:
        - **Current → target:** v1 (`tasks/`, bare `## N.`, `TSK-NN`, operator-prose) → v2 (co-located
          `specs/`, anchored sections, `<ACR>-<slug>` IDs, compressed decisions, flat-Russian).
        - **Passes:** how many iterations the run will take.
        - **Move map:** each `tasks/<scope>/<module>/…` → its co-located `specs/<scope>/<module>/…`
          destination + the `*.3-tasks.md` indexes to be built.
        - **ID map (preview):** `TSK-NN → <ACR>-<slug>` for every ticket (drafted from `Meta.Purpose`).
        - **Decision compression:** which `D-NNN` / discussion threads converged and will be merged.
        - **Files touched:** specs, tickets, AND code (ID/decision references), with a count.
        - **Optimizations:** what gets collapsed / simplified beyond a 1:1 copy.
        Then an acknowledgement check — the operator confirms «ознакомился» or adds a custom instruction
        (a scope to skip, a naming preference, a decision to keep). `H_OPERATOR_REJECTS_PLAN` on decline. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_ANCHORS">
      <Goal>Make v1 tickets visible to the v2 tools.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run `sdd-migrate anchors --all --write` (deterministic — wraps canonical sections in
        `<!--SECTION:-->` markers; idempotent, skips already-anchored). Verify with `sdd-check` (anchor
        balance clean).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_SLUG_MAP">
      <Goal>Draft the semantic ID map and get approval.</Goal>
      <Action>
        For each Task-ID, read its `Meta.Purpose` and propose `<ACR>-<slug>` — `<ACR>` the scope/module
        acronym, `<slug>` a short kebab feature name, unique within the scope (a Slug Registry; the same
        slug twice = «one feature»). Present the full map for approval; fold in any custom instruction
        from STEP_1. STOP for approval.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_ID_REPLACE">
      <Goal>Replace IDs across specs, tickets, and code — safely.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Apply the approved map ONLY: replace each exact old ID on a word boundary, across
        `specs / tasks / cli / shared / services / ai`. Never blind-replace a general `TSK-[0-9]+`
        pattern; never touch what is not an ID — `D-NNN` (spec-local, kept), `FR-NN` / `NFC-NN` /
        scope-prefixed requirement IDs (kept), and non-IDs like `UTF-8` / `UTF-16`. Verify: zero original
        Task-IDs remain (per family) and `sdd-check` clean.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_RESTRUCTURE">
      <Goal>Move tickets co-located and build the indexes (destructive — gated).</Goal>
      <Action>
        With approval (this moves files): `git mv` each anchored, slug-named ticket from
        `tasks/<scope>/<module>/` to co-located `specs/<scope>/<module>/`; assemble the
        `*.3-tasks.md` indexes from the old `tasks/<scope>/README.md` trackers
        (`SCOPE_TASKS_INDEX_STRUCTURE` / `MODULE_TASKS_INDEX_STRUCTURE`); remove the emptied `tasks/`.
        Verify `sdd-state` → `FLOW_VERSION=v2`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_COMPRESS">
      <Goal>Collapse redundant decisions and discussions (not a mechanical copy).</Goal>
      <Action>
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/compression.directive.xml")` over the migrated
        specs/tickets: cluster decisions (`D-NNN`) and discussion threads, merge those that converged on
        the same conclusion into one current statement (superseded marked per
        `AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`, never silently dropped), and propagate the merges to code
        references. Agent drafts, operator approves.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_7_LANGUAGE">
      <Goal>Operator-prose → flat engineering Russian.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Rewrite Vision, ticket prose, reports, halt messages, and BDD scenario bodies to flat
        engineering Russian: no metaphors, no English calques («подтверждение» not «аппрув»; «текст» not
        «проза»); code, IDs, status tokens, BDD keywords, and paths stay English. Agent drafts the
        candidate list (transliterated anglicisms), operator approves the rewrite.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_8_VERIFY">
      <Goal>Prove the migration is complete.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Final gate: `sdd-state` → `FLOW_VERSION=v2`; `sdd-check --all` clean; zero original Task-IDs /
        `*.task-*.md` names remain. All three green → done, return control to the caller (script readiness
        is the router's separate gate — the readiness flow handles it next). Otherwise `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL` —
        report the gap, leave the git baseline for rollback.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ReferenceData>
    **What changes:** `tasks/<scope>/<module>/<m>.task-NN.md` → co-located `specs/<scope>/<module>/` +
    `*.3-tasks.md` indexes · `TSK-NN` (or `<ACR>-NNN`) → `<ACR>-<slug>` · tickets gain `<!--SECTION:-->`
    anchors · operator-prose → flat Russian · redundant decisions collapsed.

    **What is NOT touched:** `D-NNN` (decision IDs, spec-local) stay · `FR-NN` / `NFC-NN` and
    scope-prefixed requirement/scenario IDs stay (optional later reformat to BDD `<ACR>-REQ-N`) ·
    `UTF-8` / `UTF-16` and similar are NOT IDs — never replaced.

    **Tooling state:** anchoring is a real tool (`sdd-migrate anchors`). ID-replace and move are done by
    safe, deterministic recipes today (exact IDs from the approved map, on word boundaries, UTF-safe);
    `sdd-migrate ids --map` / `move` tool-modes will replace those recipes when built — the procedure
    and its safety constraints do not change.
  </ReferenceData>

